window.__CAPM_DATA=(window.__CAPM_DATA||"")+"rs in an open-space work environment. While working on an offer, the potential client called to request a cost estimate. The project manager informed the client that it was around $600,000. However, a team member immediately corrected the project manager, saying “It’s actually around $700,000”. The project manager didn’t realize that the team member was overhearing the discussion. What kind of communication is being used here?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Open space communication<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Open space communication\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Distracting communication<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Distracting communication\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Indirect communication<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Indirect communication\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Osmotic communication<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Osmotic communication\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Osmotic communication is when team members are in the same room and one person asks a question, others in the room can either contribute to the discussion or continue working (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 243).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Osmotic communication is when team members are in the same room and one person asks a question, others in the room can either contribute to the discussion or continue working (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 243).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":133,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">A project manager is assigned to a university complex project that consists of designing and producing 200 wayfinding and directional signs. These signs will be placed and installed near doors, exits, offices, elevators, etc. by another company. After getting the client's approval that the project scope is met, the project manager delivers the signs to the installation company. The latter asks the project manager to help them with the signs’ installation. What should the project manager do? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is assigned to a university complex project that consists of designing and producing 200 wayfinding and directional signs. These signs will be placed and installed near doors, exits, offices, elevators, etc. by another company. After getting the client's approval that the project scope is met, the project manager delivers the signs to the installation company. The latter asks the project manager to help them with the signs’ installation. What should the project manager do?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>Submit a change request to assist with the signs’ installation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Submit a change request to assist with the signs’ installation\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Do a favor for the installation company and help them out<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Do a favor for the installation company and help them out\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Create a new separate project charter for the signs installation support to make it clear that it’s not part of the initial project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Create a new separate project charter for the signs installation support to make it clear that it’s not part of the initial project\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Do nothing since the project scope has been officially fulfilled and approved by the client<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Do nothing since the project scope has been officially fulfilled and approved by the client\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2A1-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A3-0\\\">Since they completed their project, which clearly consists of only designing, producing, and delivering the sign, and after getting the client’s official approval of the project's deliverables, the project manager's mission is done. They’re not part of the signs installation process therefore no further steps are required.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A5-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The signs production project is completed therefore submitting a change request doesn’t make sense.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A5-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> A company is already assigned to install the signs so there is no need to create a new project charter.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Since they completed their project, which clearly consists of only designing, producing, and delivering the sign, and after getting the client’s official approval of the project's deliverables, the project manager's mission is done. They’re not part of the signs installation process therefore no further steps are required. Option A: The signs production project is completed therefore submitting a change request doesn’t make sense. Option C: A company is already assigned to install the signs so there is no need to create a new project charter.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":134,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">One month into execution, a project’s cost variance reached $0.90. What is the project’s status?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"One month into execution, a project’s cost variance reached $0.90. What is the project’s status?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project is under budget<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The project is under budget\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project is over budget<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The project is over budget\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project will end up costing more than initially forecasted<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The project will end up costing more than initially forecasted\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project will end up costing less than initially forecasted<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The project will end up costing less than initially forecasted\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The cost variance is the difference between the earned value (EV), i.e., the budgeted cost of work performed, and actual costs (AC).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">CV = EV – AC<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">If the variance is negative, the project is over budget and if the variance is positive, it is under budget. In the question, the cost variance is barely above 0, so the project is under budget. Since the variance is very close to 0 (90 cents), we can also consider the project to be on budget, but this was not included as an option. Cost variance helps to determine the project’s current status, but it cannot determine or predict if the project will end up costing less or more than anticipated. For instance, when the CV is negative, the project manager could take preventive or corrective actions in order to steer the project back on track within the defined budget.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The cost variance is the difference between the earned value (EV), i.e., the budgeted cost of work performed, and actual costs (AC). CV = EV – AC If the variance is negative, the project is over budget and if the variance is positive, it is under budget. In the question, the cost variance is barely above 0, so the project is under budget. Since the variance is very close to 0 (90 cents), we can also consider the project to be on budget, but this was not included as an option. Cost variance helps to determine the project’s current status, but it cannot determine or predict if the project will end up costing less or more than anticipated. For instance, when the CV is negative, the project manager could take preventive or corrective actions in order to steer the project back on track within the defined budget.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":135,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which of the following statements is true regarding the project management plan?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following statements is true regarding the project management plan?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It identifies and authorizes the Project Manager to launch the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. It identifies and authorizes the Project Manager to launch the project\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It is a detailed project schedule defining the tasks and their dependencies, as well as key milestones<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. It is a detailed project schedule defining the tasks and their dependencies, as well as key milestones\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It is a formal document that defines how the project will be managed<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. It is a formal document that defines how the project will be managed\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It is part of the “Executing” process group<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. It is part of the “Executing” process group\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A project management plan is a formal document that defines how a project is going to be carried out (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 186). The project plan is created during the planning phase of the project life cycle, and it must be approved by stakeholders before the project can move on to execution.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The project charter is a document that is meant to identify and authorize the Project Manager to start the project<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The project management plan is created as part of the planning process group.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C A project management plan is a formal document that defines how a project is going to be carried out (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 186). The project plan is created during the planning phase of the project life cycle, and it must be approved by stakeholders before the project can move on to execution. Option A: The project charter is a document that is meant to identify and authorize the Project Manager to start the project . Option D: The project management plan is created as part of the planning process group.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":136,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">An organization has decided to create an innovative system for product quality control. The project manager assigned to this project chose an Agile approach. Why did the project manager make this choice?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"An organization has decided to create an innovative system for product quality control. The project manager assigned to this project chose an Agile approach. Why did the project manager make this choice?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To avoid change requests as much as possible<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. To avoid change requests as much as possible\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To avoid scope creep as much as possible<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. To avoid scope creep as much as possible\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To get feedback as early as possible<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. To get feedback as early as possible\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>To complete the project as early as possible<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. To complete the project as early as possible\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Since it’s based on short development iterations, Agile approaches allow for early and frequent feedback by delivering a working piece of the product at the end of each iteration to the customer. Since traditional projects can only obtain customer feedback at the end, it is often too late to incorporate the feedback or fix any issues at that stage, unlike Agile projects where new changes are welcomed and integrated into the product development process.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Since it’s based on short development iterations, Agile approaches allow for early and frequent feedback by delivering a working piece of the product at the end of each iteration to the customer. Since traditional projects can only obtain customer feedback at the end, it is often too late to incorporate the feedback or fix any issues at that stage, unlike Agile projects where new changes are welcomed and integrated into the product development process.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":137,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which of the following best describes the Definition of Done (DoD)?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following best describes the Definition of Done (DoD)?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Is a set of criteria that must be met before a product or feature can be considered complete, and it is agreed upon by the delivery team and the product owner (PO).<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Is a set of criteria that must be met before a product or feature can be considered complete, and it is agreed upon by the delivery team and the product owner (PO).\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Outlines the criteria that must be met before a product backlog item is considered ready to be worked on by the team.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Outlines the criteria that must be met before a product backlog item is considered ready to be worked on by the team.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Refers to the expectations for releases within the time frame shown on the roadmap, focusing on continual improvement of the product and process.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Refers to the expectations for releases within the time frame shown on the roadmap, focusing on continual improvement of the product and process.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Is used to review the product and process to identify areas for improvement through methods such as surveys, interviews, and usability testing.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Is used to review the product and process to identify areas for improvement through methods such as surveys, interviews, and usability testing.\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The DoD is a set of criteria that must be met for a product or feature to be considered complete, ensuring it meets the agreed-upon standards for quality and functionality.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The Definition of Ready (DoR) is about preparing backlog items for development, ensuring they are well-defined and actionable before work begins.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Expectations for releases is related to release planning rather than the Definition of Done. The DoD is specifically about when an individual product increment or feature is considered complete, not about the timing or continuous improvement expectations for releases.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Reviewing the product and process related to demo and retrospective meetings, which are used to improve both the product and the process by gathering feedback.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The DoD is a set of criteria that must be met for a product or feature to be considered complete, ensuring it meets the agreed-upon standards for quality and functionality. Option B: The Definition of Ready (DoR) is about preparing backlog items for development, ensuring they are well-defined and actionable before work begins. Option C: Expectations for releases is related to release planning rather than the Definition of Done. The DoD is specifically about when an individual product increment or feature is considered complete, not about the timing or continuous improvement expectations for releases. Option D: Reviewing the product and process related to demo and retrospective meetings, which are used to improve both the product and the process by gathering feedback.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":138,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">While examining their project progress, a project manager finds out that the schedule variance is $0.00. Which of the following statements is true about this project? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"While examining their project progress, a project manager finds out that the schedule variance is $0.00. Which of the following statements is true about this project?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3C-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project’s CPI equals 1 <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The project’s CPI equals 1\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project’s EV equals its PV <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The project’s EV equals its PV\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project’s cost variance is $0.00 too <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The project’s cost variance is $0.00 too\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project’s EAC equals its BAC <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The project’s EAC equals its BAC\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = B<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">Schedule variance (SV) measures whether your project is on track by calculating its actual progress against expected progress to determine how ahead of or behind schedule the project work is. SV equals the difference between your project’s earned value and planned value: SV = EV – PV. Therefore, an SV of $0.00 means that the project’s EV equals its PV. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Schedule variance (SV) measures whether your project is on track by calculating its actual progress against expected progress to determine how ahead of or behind schedule the project work is. SV equals the difference between your project’s earned value and planned value: SV = EV – PV. Therefore, an SV of $0.00 means that the project’s EV equals its PV.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":139,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">A project manager is assigned to a network upgrade project. After the project scope approval, the Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) can now be created. Who is in charge of creating the WBS? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is assigned to a network upgrade project. After the project scope approval, the Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) can now be created. Who is in charge of creating the WBS?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>The project sponsor<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The project sponsor\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The project manager\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project team<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The project team\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The product owner<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The product owner\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = C<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">The project team is responsible for carrying out the process of creating the project Work Breakdown Structure (WBS). Involving all stakeholders in the creation of the WBS can be both unrealistic and impractical since certain projects can include hundreds and even thousands of stakeholders. Plus, even if they were included, they would most likely lack the necessary skills to contribute to the creation of the WBS. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The project manager is partially involved in the process and not responsible for performing it: they can only facilitate the WBS creation and provide the team with the needed help and direction. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The project team is responsible for carrying out the process of creating the project Work Breakdown Structure (WBS). Involving all stakeholders in the creation of the WBS can be both unrealistic and impractical since certain projects can include hundreds and even thousands of stakeholders. Plus, even if they were included, they would most likely lack the necessary skills to contribute to the creation of the WBS. Option B: The project manager is partially involved in the process and not responsible for performing it: they can only facilitate the WBS creation and provide the team with the needed help and direction.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":140,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">This is a project manager’s first time leading an agile project. Knowing that they opted for the Scrum framework, which of the following describes the project team?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"This is a project manager’s first time leading an agile project. Knowing that they opted for the Scrum framework, which of the following describes the project team?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The team size ranges from three to nine members<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The team size ranges from three to nine members\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>All of the team members have a technical background<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. All of the team members have a technical background\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>All of the team members are I-shaped<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. All of the team members are I-shaped\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>All of the team members are dependent on the Scrum maste<span><\\/span>r<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. All of the team members are dependent on the Scrum maste r\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The typical size of an agile team ranges from three to nine members<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Options B &amp; D:<\\/span> Agile teams should be multidisciplinary (not necessarily have a technical background) and self-organizing (not dependent on the scrum master).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Successful agile teams are made up of generalizing specialists/T-shaped members who have deep knowledge in one area and a broad ability in other areas. I-shaped, on the other hand, refers to a person with a profound knowledge of one area but has no interest or skill in other areas (Agile Practice Guide, page 42).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The typical size of an agile team ranges from three to nine members . Options B & D: Agile teams should be multidisciplinary (not necessarily have a technical background) and self-organizing (not dependent on the scrum master). Option C: Successful agile teams are made up of generalizing specialists/T-shaped members who have deep knowledge in one area and a broad ability in other areas. I-shaped, on the other hand, refers to a person with a profound knowledge of one area but has no interest or skill in other areas (Agile Practice Guide, page 42).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":141,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">What is the primary purpose of Kano analysis?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is the primary purpose of Kano analysis?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>To assess the technical feasibility of product features.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"To assess the technical feasibility of product features.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>To determine the cost-effectiveness of product development.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"To determine the cost-effectiveness of product development.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>To understand customer preferences and priorities.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"To understand customer preferences and priorities.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>To measure the overall market demand for a product.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"To measure the overall market demand for a product.\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Kano analysis is designed to model and analyze product features from the customer's perspective. It helps product teams understand how different features are valued by customers, which aids in prioritizing them. During Kano analysis, features are categorized and plotted on a grid to determine their importance and impact on customer satisfaction. This method allows teams to focus on features that will have the most significant effect on customer satisfaction and prioritize development accordingly (PMI guide to business analysis, page 79).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Kano analysis is designed to model and analyze product features from the customer's perspective. It helps product teams understand how different features are valued by customers, which aids in prioritizing them. During Kano analysis, features are categorized and plotted on a grid to determine their importance and impact on customer satisfaction. This method allows teams to focus on features that will have the most significant effect on customer satisfaction and prioritize development accordingly (PMI guide to business analysis, page 79).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":142,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">A project manager is acquiring a team for a new project. A candidate for a particular position assures the project manager that he would be a great asset to the project team. The candidate adds that if the project manager hires him, he will give the latter any project bonus he might receive. What should the project manager do? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is acquiring a team for a new project. A candidate for a particular position assures the project manager that he would be a great asset to the project team. The candidate adds that if the project manager hires him, he will give the latter any project bonus he might receive. What should the project manager do?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>Consider the candidate’s statement a joke<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Consider the candidate’s statement a joke\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>End the job interview straightaway<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. End the job interview straightaway\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Reject the candidate's job application<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Reject the candidate's job application\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Accept the candidate’s offer and hire him<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Accept the candidate’s offer and hire him\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = C<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">The best thing to do in this situation is to reject the candidate's job application. Apart from being unethical, offering or accepting a bribe is a huge violation of the PMI Code of Ethics. Even if the candidate was joking, this type of joke is inappropriate and an indication of his lack of professionalism. The project manager should avoid the fuss of ending the job interview straightaway and just reject the application later on. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The best thing to do in this situation is to reject the candidate's job application. Apart from being unethical, offering or accepting a bribe is a huge violation of the PMI Code of Ethics. Even if the candidate was joking, this type of joke is inappropriate and an indication of his lack of professionalism. The project manager should avoid the fuss of ending the job interview straightaway and just reject the application later on.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":143,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">Which of the following statements about Risk Management is the most accurate? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following statements about Risk Management is the most accurate?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3C-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Identified risks should be included in the risk register <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Identified risks should be included in the risk register\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Identified risks should be included in the Risk Management Plan <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Identified risks should be included in the Risk Management Plan\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A risk that cannot be mitigated must be avoided <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. A risk that cannot be mitigated must be avoided\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A risk that cannot be avoided must be mitigated <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. A risk that cannot be avoided must be mitigated\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = A<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">All identified risks should be added to the risk register. The risk register includes identified project risks, risk owners, agreed-upon risk responses, and specific implementation actions, as well as other details including control actions for assessing the effectiveness of response plans, signs of risk, residual and secondary risks, and a watch list of low-priority risks. Risk responses include: Avoid, Escalate, Transfer, Mitigate, and Accept (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 123). <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Options C &amp; D:<\\/span> A risk that cannot be mitigated or avoided could be escalated, transferred, or accepted. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A All identified risks should be added to the risk register. The risk register includes identified project risks, risk owners, agreed-upon risk responses, and specific implementation actions, as well as other details including control actions for assessing the effectiveness of response plans, signs of risk, residual and secondary risks, and a watch list of low-priority risks. Risk responses include: Avoid, Escalate, Transfer, Mitigate, and Accept (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 123). Options C & D: A risk that cannot be mitigated or avoided could be escalated, transferred, or accepted.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":144,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager was recently hired by an organization. In their previous position, the project manager used to have wide-ranging authority. Wondering if things would be different for them in the new organization, the project manager asked their mentor what type of organization it was. Which of the following options is not an organizational structure type?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager was recently hired by an organization. In their previous position, the project manager used to have wide-ranging authority. Wondering if things would be different for them in the new organization, the project manager asked their mentor what type of organization it was. Which of the following options is not an organizational structure type?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Projectized<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Projectized\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Matrix<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Matrix\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Functional<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Functional\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Technical<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Technical\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Technical is not an organizational structure. There are multiple types of organizational structures including functional or centralized, matrix, and projectized or project-oriented.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Technical is not an organizational structure. There are multiple types of organizational structures including functional or centralized, matrix, and projectized or project-oriented.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":145,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A Product Owner at a tech company developing a new project management tool. The Product Owner is currently in the process of creating the product roadmap with the help of the business analyst, which will guide the development team and stakeholders on the product’s direction over the next few quarters. Which of the following components should the product owner include in the product roadmap? (Select three)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A Product Owner at a tech company developing a new project management tool. The Product Owner is currently in the process of creating the product roadmap with the help of the business analyst, which will guide the development team and stakeholders on the product’s direction over the next few quarters. Which of the following components should the product owner include in the product roadmap? (Select three)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Communication channels<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Communication channels\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Product status<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Product status\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Product visio<span><\\/span>n<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Product visio n\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Features<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Features\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Timeline<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Timeline\"}],\"key\":[\"C\",\"D\",\"E\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C, D, E<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9D-0\\\">Product vision is the description of the product’s long-term objectives. The product roadmap should include the identification of the key features that will be developed for the product. Typically the features are grouped by release or a development approach. The timeline provides a detailed schedule for the product's development, highlighting key milestones and deadlines for feature releases<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C, D, E Product vision is the description of the product’s long-term objectives. The product roadmap should include the identification of the key features that will be developed for the product. Typically the features are grouped by release or a development approach. The timeline provides a detailed schedule for the product's development, highlighting key milestones and deadlines for feature releases .\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":3},{\"n\":146,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sTU-1\\\">Match the following techniques with the corresponding description in the table below: <span>Brainstorming<\\/span> - <span>Benchmarking<\\/span> - <span>Focus group<\\/span> - <span>Nominal group<\\/span><\\/p><div class=\\\"class_sFS-0\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/div>\",\"stemText\":\"Match the following techniques with the corresponding description in the table below: Brainstorming - Benchmarking - Focus group - Nominal group\",\"choices\":[],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\">●<span>        <\\/span><span>A.<\\/span><span> <\\/span><span>Focus groups:<\\/span> involve an interactive group discussion facilitated by a moderator<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\">●<span>        <\\/span><span>B. Brainstorming:<\\/span> a group discussion to quickly generate a large number of ideas<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\">●<span>        <\\/span><span>C. Nominal group:<\\/span> a group discussion to produce ideas and prioritize them through voting<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\">●<span>        <\\/span><span>D. Benchmarking:<\\/span> involves a comparison of ideas, products, processes, practices, etc.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B ● A. Focus groups: involve an interactive group discussion facilitated by a moderator ● B. Brainstorming: a group discussion to quickly generate a large number of ideas ● C. Nominal group: a group discussion to produce ideas and prioritize them through voting ● D. Benchmarking: involves a comparison of ideas, products, processes, practices, etc.\",\"type\":\"mapping\",\"special\":{\"type\":\"mapping\",\"targets\":[[\"A\",\"A. Interactive group discussion facilitated by a moderator\"],[\"B\",\"B. Group discussion to quickly generate a large number of ideas\"],[\"C\",\"C. Group discussion to produce ideas and prioritize them through voting\"],[\"D\",\"D. Comparison of ideas, products, processes, practices, etc.\"]],\"options\":[[\"brainstorming\",\"Brainstorming\"],[\"benchmarking\",\"Benchmarking\"],[\"focus-group\",\"Focus group\"],[\"nominal-group\",\"Nominal group\"]],\"correct\":{\"A\":\"focus-group\",\"B\":\"brainstorming\",\"C\":\"nominal-group\",\"D\":\"benchmarking\"},\"note\":\"Source inconsistency: the answer line says “Correct Answer = B”, while the explanation immediately maps all four rows (A = Focus groups, B = Brainstorming, C = Nominal group, D = Benchmarking). This app grades the matching interaction against that source explanation and shows the original answer block unchanged in review.\"},\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"Source inconsistency: the answer line says “Correct Answer = B”, while the explanation immediately maps all four rows (A = Focus groups, B = Brainstorming, C = Nominal group, D = Benchmarking). This app grades the matching interaction against that source explanation and shows the original answer block unchanged in review.\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":147,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">A project manager signs a contract worth millions of dollars to manage a 4-month international sports event. During the planning phase, the project manager discovers a serious threat to the project; one of their contractors might declare bankruptcy. If that happens, the project will be delayed for another two months. After giving it some thought, the project manager decides to contact another contractor who can supply the necessary materials. This is an example of: <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager signs a contract worth millions of dollars to manage a 4-month international sports event. During the planning phase, the project manager discovers a serious threat to the project; one of their contractors might declare bankruptcy. If that happens, the project will be delayed for another two months. After giving it some thought, the project manager decides to contact another contractor who can supply the necessary materials. This is an example of:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3C-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Contract breach <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Contract breach\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Risk Transfer <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Risk Transfer\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Risk Acceptance <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Risk Acceptance\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Risk Mitigation <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Risk Mitigation\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = D<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">The described situation depicts Risk Mitigation. The project manager did not cancel the contract because the contractor might go bankrupt. They did not breach the contract either by getting in touch with another supplier. They contacted a different vendor in order to keep their options open and have other alternatives in case the risk occurs. By doing this, the possibility of the project’s delay is reduced. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D The described situation depicts Risk Mitigation. The project manager did not cancel the contract because the contractor might go bankrupt. They did not breach the contract either by getting in touch with another supplier. They contacted a different vendor in order to keep their options open and have other alternatives in case the risk occurs. By doing this, the possibility of the project’s delay is reduced.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":148,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A business analyst is conducting a focus group to obtain direct feedback from customers and end users. Who are the primary participants in the focus groups?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A business analyst is conducting a focus group to obtain direct feedback from customers and end users. Who are the primary participants in the focus groups?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Subject matter experts (SMEs)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Subject matter experts (SMEs)\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Project manager\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project team<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Project team\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project sponsor<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Project sponsor\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9D-0\\\">Subject matter experts (SMEs) are a valuable source for product-related information, providing insights and expectations of the future state. Subject matter experts (SMEs) can be long-time members of the product development team.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Subject matter experts (SMEs) are a valuable source for product-related information, providing insights and expectations of the future state. Subject matter experts (SMEs) can be long-time members of the product development team.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":149,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">Which of the following options are conflict-resolution techniques? (Select three) <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following options are conflict-resolution techniques? (Select three)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3C-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Smoothing <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Smoothing\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Forcing <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Forcing\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Adjourning <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Adjourning\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Withdrawing <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Withdrawing\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"B\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = A, B, D<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">Conflict resolution techniques include withdrawal/avoiding, smoothing/accommodating, compromising, forcing, collaborating, and problem-solving/confronting (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 169). <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Adjourning is one of the five stages of team development according to the Tuckman ladder. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, B, D Conflict resolution techniques include withdrawal/avoiding, smoothing/accommodating, compromising, forcing, collaborating, and problem-solving/confronting (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 169). Option C: Adjourning is one of the five stages of team development according to the Tuckman ladder.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":3},{\"n\":150,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">In the adaptive approach, acceptance criteria are used for:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In the adaptive approach, acceptance criteria are used for:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Defining the overall product vision<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Defining the overall product vision\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Writing user stories<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Writing user stories\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Measuring project progress<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Measuring project progress\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>Managing risks<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Managing risks\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Acceptance criteria specify the conditions that a product or feature must meet to be considered complete and acceptable. They are integral to writing user stories in an adaptive or Agile approach, as they provide clear and testable requirements that guide the development process and ensure that user stories are correctly implemented (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 227).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Acceptance criteria specify the conditions that a product or feature must meet to be considered complete and acceptable. They are integral to writing user stories in an adaptive or Agile approach, as they provide clear and testable requirements that guide the development process and ensure that user stories are correctly implemented (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 227).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null}]},{\"id\":\"mock-3\",\"title\":\"Full Mock Exam 3\",\"kind\":\"Full Mock Exam\",\"count\":150,\"questions\":[{\"n\":1,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A project manager joined a new project and wanted to check the roles and responsibilities of the project team, their hierarchical links, and how they should be managed. What should the project manager refer to?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager joined a new project and wanted to check the roles and responsibilities of the project team, their hierarchical links, and how they should be managed. What should the project manager refer to?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Resource Management Plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Resource Management Plan\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Resource Breakdown Structure<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Resource Breakdown Structure\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>RACI chart<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. RACI chart\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Resource leveling<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Resource leveling\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A The Resource Management Plan is where the approach to handling and structuring roles, responsibilities, and team management in a project is documented.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Resource Breakdown Structure could be part of the ​​Resource Management Plan and it shows the hierarchical links only, not the way the project team is managed.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> RACI is used to assign roles to team members, and it doesn’t describe the way the project team is managed.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Resource leveling is a resource management technique that is used to accommodate resource constraints in order to predict project timelines.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The Resource Management Plan is where the approach to handling and structuring roles, responsibilities, and team management in a project is documented. Option B: Resource Breakdown Structure could be part of the Resource Management Plan and it shows the hierarchical links only, not the way the project team is managed. Option C: RACI is used to assign roles to team members, and it doesn’t describe the way the project team is managed. Option D: Resource leveling is a resource management technique that is used to accommodate resource constraints in order to predict project timelines.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":2,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>The process of identifying and documenting the relationships between project activities is called:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The process of identifying and documenting the relationships between project activities is called:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Control the Schedule<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Control the Schedule\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sequence Activities<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Sequence Activities\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Define Activities<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Define Activities\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Develop Schedule<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Develop Schedule\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B Sequencing activities involves identifying and documenting the logical relationships among project activities.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Controlling the schedule is about managing schedule changes, not identifying relationships.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Defining activities involves breaking down work packages into tasks but not establishing relationships.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Developing the schedule comes after sequencing activities.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Sequencing activities involves identifying and documenting the logical relationships among project activities. Option A: Controlling the schedule is about managing schedule changes, not identifying relationships. Option C: Defining activities involves breaking down work packages into tasks but not establishing relationships. Option D: Developing the schedule comes after sequencing activities.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":3,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A project team faced certain conditions that were beyond their control which influenced the project plan and execution. What are these conditions called?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project team faced certain conditions that were beyond their control which influenced the project plan and execution. What are these conditions called?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Work performance reports<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Work performance reports\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Enterprise Environmental Factors<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Enterprise Environmental Factors\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Organizational Process Assets<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Organizational Process Assets\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Risks<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Risks\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B Enterprise Environmental Factors (EEFs) are conditions not under the control of the project team that can influence or constrain the project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Work performance reports provide information on project performance, not conditions influencing it.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Organizational process assets include policies, procedures, and knowledge bases, which are within the organization's control.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Risks are not always beyond the control of the project team; some risks could be mitigated, while others could be even avoided.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Enterprise Environmental Factors (EEFs) are conditions not under the control of the project team that can influence or constrain the project. Option A: Work performance reports provide information on project performance, not conditions influencing it. Option C: Organizational process assets include policies, procedures, and knowledge bases, which are within the organization's control. Option D: Risks are not always beyond the control of the project team; some risks could be mitigated, while others could be even avoided.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":4,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">When is the most appropriate time for an agile team to review the Definition of Done?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"When is the most appropriate time for an agile team to review the Definition of Done?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>During the Sprint Planning<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. During the Sprint Planning\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Before starting a new Sprint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Before starting a new Sprint\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>During the Sprint Retrospective<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. During the Sprint Retrospective\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Before starting a new project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Before starting a new project\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>During the Sprint Review<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. During the Sprint Review\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Definition of Done is a checklist of the activities that the team is expected to successfully complete before it can declare its work to be “done”. The product owner and the development team agree upon <span><\\/span>the details of the Definition of Done in order to clarify what shippability means and the work each user story requires.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">During the Sprint Retrospective, the team inspects how the last Sprint went with regard to individuals, interactions, processes, tools, and Definition of Done.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Definition of Done is a checklist of the activities that the team is expected to successfully complete before it can declare its work to be “done”. The product owner and the development team agree upon the details of the Definition of Done in order to clarify what shippability means and the work each user story requires. During the Sprint Retrospective, the team inspects how the last Sprint went with regard to individuals, interactions, processes, tools, and Definition of Done.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":5,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Between two Sprints, what activities would a Product Owner typically undertake?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Between two Sprints, what activities would a Product Owner typically undertake?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Refine the Product Backlog<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Refine the Product Backlog\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Update the project plan with stakeholders<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Update the project plan with stakeholders\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>There is no time between Sprints; the next Sprint starts immediately after the current Sprint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. There is no time between Sprints; the next Sprint starts immediately after the current Sprint\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Complete the report for the previous Sprint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Complete the report for the previous Sprint\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C A sprint is an event that has a fixed duration of one month or less to create consistency. A new Sprint starts immediately after the conclusion of the previous Sprint.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C A sprint is an event that has a fixed duration of one month or less to create consistency. A new Sprint starts immediately after the conclusion of the previous Sprint.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":6,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which statement is true about a portfolio ?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which statement is true about a portfolio ?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It consists of unrelated projects, programs, and operational work aimed at achieving strategic objectives.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. It consists of unrelated projects, programs, and operational work aimed at achieving strategic objectives.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It involves managing interrelated projects that have a common objective.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. It involves managing interrelated projects that have a common objective.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It focuses solely on completing temporary endeavors with defined outcomes.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. It focuses solely on completing temporary endeavors with defined outcomes.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It is concerned only with individual project completion and resource allocation.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. It is concerned only with individual project completion and resource allocation.\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A A portfolio is a collection of projects, programs, and operational work that are managed together to achieve strategic business goals. These projects and programs do not necessarily have to be related or interdependent; rather, they are grouped to align with an organization&#x27;s broader objectives.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> “It involves managing interrelated projects that have a common objective” refers to a program rather than a portfolio.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> “It focuses solely on completing temporary endeavors with defined outcomes” refers to a project rather than a portfolio.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> “It is concerned only with individual project completion and resource allocation” refers to project management.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A A portfolio is a collection of projects, programs, and operational work that are managed together to achieve strategic business goals. These projects and programs do not necessarily have to be related or interdependent; rather, they are grouped to align with an organization's broader objectives. Option B: “It involves managing interrelated projects that have a common objective” refers to a program rather than a portfolio. Option C: “It focuses solely on completing temporary endeavors with defined outcomes” refers to a project rather than a portfolio. Option D: “It is concerned only with individual project completion and resource allocation” refers to project management.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":7,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which of the following techniques is primarily used to evaluate and select vendors?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following techniques is primarily used to evaluate and select vendors?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Procurement Management Plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Procurement Management Plan\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Market research<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Market research\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder register<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Stakeholder register\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Source selection criteria<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Source selection criteria\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D Source Selection Criteria are developed as an output of the Plan Procurement Management process to define how buyer decisions will be made (Process groups guide, page 238).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The Procurement Management Plan describes how procurements will be conducted, and it’s not primarily used to evaluate and select vendors.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Market Research is part of the tools and techniques used in planning procurement not an output.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The Stakeholder Register is related to stakeholder management, not procurement.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Source Selection Criteria are developed as an output of the Plan Procurement Management process to define how buyer decisions will be made (Process groups guide, page 238). Option A: The Procurement Management Plan describes how procurements will be conducted, and it’s not primarily used to evaluate and select vendors. Option B: Market Research is part of the tools and techniques used in planning procurement not an output. Option C: The Stakeholder Register is related to stakeholder management, not procurement.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":8,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Who is responsible for managing the progress of work during a Sprint?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Who is responsible for managing the progress of work during a Sprint?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The Scrum Master<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The Scrum Master\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The Development Team<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The Development Team\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The Product Owner<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The Product Owner\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The Project Manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The Project Manager\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>The Functional Manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. The Functional Manager\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The Development Team uses the Daily Scrum to inspect progress toward the Sprint Goal and to inspect how progress is trending toward completing the work in the Sprint Backlog.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The Development Team uses the Daily Scrum to inspect progress toward the Sprint Goal and to inspect how progress is trending toward completing the work in the Sprint Backlog.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":9,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A business analyst is splitting a large user story into smaller, manageable parts to be delivered within a single iteration. What technique is the business analyst using?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A business analyst is splitting a large user story into smaller, manageable parts to be delivered within a single iteration. What technique is the business analyst using?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Use case<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Use case\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Story elaboration<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Story elaboration\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Story slicing<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Story slicing\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Story mapping<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Story mapping\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Story slicing is a technique used for breaking down large tasks, such as epics or user stories, into smaller, more manageable parts (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 214)<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Story slicing is a technique used for breaking down large tasks, such as epics or user stories, into smaller, more manageable parts (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 214) .\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":10,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">After the second sprint, a product owner noticed that the market needs may be changing, and the product may not fit the new market needs. What should the product owner do next?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"After the second sprint, a product owner noticed that the market needs may be changing, and the product may not fit the new market needs. What should the product owner do next?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Pause the project and report the issue to the project sponsor<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Pause the project and report the issue to the project sponsor\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Submit a formal change request to change the product scope<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Submit a formal change request to change the product scope\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Finalize the product on time and budget to launch as planned<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Finalize the product on time and budget to launch as planned\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Review and reprioritize the backlog to address the new market needs<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Review and reprioritize the backlog to address the new market needs\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The product owner should first review the backlog, which contains prioritized features and tasks, to assess how the changing market needs will impact the product. This allows for a well-informed decision on whether to adjust the product scope or continue as planned.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> It’s among the product owner's responsibilities to respond to market changes, therefore pausing the project is a very extreme case which is not appropriate as a first step.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Submitting a formal change request is related to predictive projects, not agile projects.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Finalizing the product on time and budget without addressing the changing market needs risks delivering a product that doesn’t meet market demands.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D The product owner should first review the backlog, which contains prioritized features and tasks, to assess how the changing market needs will impact the product. This allows for a well-informed decision on whether to adjust the product scope or continue as planned. Option A: It’s among the product owner's responsibilities to respond to market changes, therefore pausing the project is a very extreme case which is not appropriate as a first step. Option B: Submitting a formal change request is related to predictive projects, not agile projects. Option C: Finalizing the product on time and budget without addressing the changing market needs risks delivering a product that doesn’t meet market demands.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":11,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which document is used to ensure that each product requirement is linked to the deliverables that address it?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which document is used to ensure that each product requirement is linked to the deliverables that address it?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Requirements documentation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Requirements documentation\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Requirements Traceability Matri<span><\\/span>x<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Requirements Traceability Matri x\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Work Breakdown Structure<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Work Breakdown Structure\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scope baseline<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Scope baseline\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B The Requirements Traceability Matrix links product requirements to the deliverables that satisfy them, ensuring that each requirement is fulfilled.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Requirements Documentation describes the requirements but does not link them to deliverables.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The Requirements Traceability Matrix links product requirements to the deliverables that satisfy them, ensuring that each requirement is fulfilled. Option A: Requirements Documentation describes the requirements but does not link them to deliverables.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":12,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Units of measure, level of precision, level of accuracy, control thresholds, and performance measurement rules are examples of elements defined in:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Units of measure, level of precision, level of accuracy, control thresholds, and performance measurement rules are examples of elements defined in:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cost Management Plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Cost Management Plan\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Work Performance Information<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Work Performance Information\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Quality Management Plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Quality Management Plan\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Work Breakdown Structure (WBS)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Work Breakdown Structure (WBS)\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A These elements are defined in the Cost Management Plan, which guides how the project&#x27;s costs will be managed and controlled (PMI process groups, page 208).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Work Performance Information is data related to the performance of the project but doesn’t define these elements.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The Quality Management Plan focuses on quality requirements and standards, not cost-related elements.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) is a hierarchical decomposition of the project scope, not a plan for managing costs.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A These elements are defined in the Cost Management Plan, which guides how the project's costs will be managed and controlled (PMI process groups, page 208). Option B: Work Performance Information is data related to the performance of the project but doesn’t define these elements. Option C: The Quality Management Plan focuses on quality requirements and standards, not cost-related elements. Option D: The Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) is a hierarchical decomposition of the project scope, not a plan for managing costs.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":13,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>What type of dependency is established based on knowledge of best practices or when a specific sequence is preferred over other acceptable sequences?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What type of dependency is established based on knowledge of best practices or when a specific sequence is preferred over other acceptable sequences?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>External<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. External\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Internal<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Internal\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Mandatory<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Mandatory\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Discretionary<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Discretionary\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D Discretionary dependencies are established based on best practices or when a specific sequence is desired, even though other sequences may be acceptable.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> External dependencies involve relationships between project activities and external factors.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Internal dependencies are within the control of the project team.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Mandatory dependencies are legally or contractually required and cannot be changed<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Discretionary dependencies are established based on best practices or when a specific sequence is desired, even though other sequences may be acceptable. Option A: External dependencies involve relationships between project activities and external factors. Option B: Internal dependencies are within the control of the project team. Option C: Mandatory dependencies are legally or contractually required and cannot be changed .\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":14,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Sensitivity analysis is usually displayed in the form of:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Sensitivity analysis is usually displayed in the form of:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Decision Tree Diagram<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Decision Tree Diagram\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Tornado Diagram<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Tornado Diagram\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Pareto Diagram<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Pareto Diagram\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Fishbone Diagram<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Fishbone Diagram\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B A Tornado Diagram is a common way to display sensitivity analysis, showing the impact of changing one variable at a time on the project&#x27;s outcome.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> A Decision Tree Diagram is used for decision-making processes, not sensitivity analysis.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> A Pareto Diagram identifies the most significant factors in a dataset, not sensitivity analysis.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> A fishbone diagram is used to identify the root causes of a problem.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B A Tornado Diagram is a common way to display sensitivity analysis, showing the impact of changing one variable at a time on the project's outcome. Option A: A Decision Tree Diagram is used for decision-making processes, not sensitivity analysis. Option C: A Pareto Diagram identifies the most significant factors in a dataset, not sensitivity analysis. Option D: A fishbone diagram is used to identify the root causes of a problem.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":15,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>The control process group includes processes that:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The control process group includes processes that:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Establish the scope, objectives, and plan of action for a project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Establish the scope, objectives, and plan of action for a project.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Define a new project or a new phase of an existing project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Define a new project or a new phase of an existing project.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Track, review, and regulate the progress and performance of a project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Track, review, and regulate the progress and performance of a project.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Complete the work defined in the project management plan.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Complete the work defined in the project management plan.\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C The Control Process Group includes processes that track, review, and regulate the progress and performance of the project, ensuring that everything aligns with the project management plan.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Establishing the scope, objectives, and plan of action is part of the Planning Process Group.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Defining a new project or phase belongs to the Initiating Process Group.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Completing the work defined in the project management plan is associated with the Executing Process Group.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The Control Process Group includes processes that track, review, and regulate the progress and performance of the project, ensuring that everything aligns with the project management plan. Option A: Establishing the scope, objectives, and plan of action is part of the Planning Process Group. Option B: Defining a new project or phase belongs to the Initiating Process Group. Option D: Completing the work defined in the project management plan is associated with the Executing Process Group.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":16,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Typical project outcomes include:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Typical project outcomes include:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Products, services, and results.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Products, services, and results.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Products, programs, and services.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Products, programs, and services.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Results, portfolios, and services.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Results, portfolios, and services.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Results, processes, and products.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Results, processes, and products.\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A A project is a temporary endeavor undertaken to create a unique product, service, or result (PMI process groups, page 4).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Programs are collections of related projects, not typical project outcomes.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Portfolios are collections of projects or programs, they cannot be a project outcome.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Processes are steps or methods used within a project, not final outcomes.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A A project is a temporary endeavor undertaken to create a unique product, service, or result (PMI process groups, page 4). Option B: Programs are collections of related projects, not typical project outcomes. Option C: Portfolios are collections of projects or programs, they cannot be a project outcome. Option D: Processes are steps or methods used within a project, not final outcomes.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":17,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>What communication technique does a project manager use to create consensus and overcome obstacles ?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What communication technique does a project manager use to create consensus and overcome obstacles ?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Listening<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Listening\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Facilitation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Facilitation\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Meeting Management<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Meeting Management\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Nonverbal communication<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Nonverbal communication\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B Facilitation is a key communication technique used by project managers to create consensus and overcome obstacles during project discussions and decision-making processes.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Listening is a crucial skill but is not a technique for creating consensus.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Meeting Management is about organizing and running meetings effectively but does not specifically focus on creating consensus.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Nonverbal communication is used to convey information through facial expressions, gestures, and body posture or position, not to create consensus<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Facilitation is a key communication technique used by project managers to create consensus and overcome obstacles during project discussions and decision-making processes. Option A: Listening is a crucial skill but is not a technique for creating consensus. Option C: Meeting Management is about organizing and running meetings effectively but does not specifically focus on creating consensus. Option D: Nonverbal communication is used to convey information through facial expressions, gestures, and body posture or position, not to create consensus .\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":18,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>When does the project team determine which dependencies are discretionary?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"When does the project team determine which dependencies are discretionary?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Before the Define Activities process<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Before the Define Activities process\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>During the Define Activities process<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. During the Define Activities process\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Before the Sequence Activities process<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Before the Sequence Activities process\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>During the Sequence Activities process<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. During the Sequence Activities process\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D The project team determines discretionary dependencies during the Sequence Activities process. Discretionary dependencies are established based on best practices or preferences.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Determining dependencies before defining activities is not practical as activities are not yet clearly identified.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> During the Define Activities process, activities are identified but dependencies are not yet determined.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Dependencies are not typically determined before sequencing activities, as sequencing is when relationships are established.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D The project team determines discretionary dependencies during the Sequence Activities process. Discretionary dependencies are established based on best practices or preferences. Option A: Determining dependencies before defining activities is not practical as activities are not yet clearly identified. Option B: During the Define Activities process, activities are identified but dependencies are not yet determined. Option C: Dependencies are not typically determined before sequencing activities, as sequencing is when relationships are established.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":19,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A project manager wants to check the resources linked to work packages. What should the project manager refer to?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager wants to check the resources linked to work packages. What should the project manager refer to?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Work Breakdown Structure<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Work Breakdown Structure\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Responsibility Assignment Matrix<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Responsibility Assignment Matrix\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Resource Breakdown Structure<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Resource Breakdown Structure\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Resource Management Plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Resource Management Plan\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B The Responsibility Assignment Matrix (RAM), or RACI chart, shows resources linked to work packages, outlining who is responsible, accountable, consulted, and informed for each task.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) shows the hierarchical breakdown of the project's scope but does not link resources to work packages.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The Resource Breakdown Structure (RBS) lists resources by category and type, not by work packages.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The Resource Management Plan describes how resources will be acquired, managed, and released. It doesn’t show the link between work packages and resources.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The Responsibility Assignment Matrix (RAM), or RACI chart, shows resources linked to work packages, outlining who is responsible, accountable, consulted, and informed for each task. Option A: The Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) shows the hierarchical breakdown of the project's scope but does not link resources to work packages. Option C: The Resource Breakdown Structure (RBS) lists resources by category and type, not by work packages. Option D: The Resource Management Plan describes how resources will be acquired, managed, and released. It doesn’t show the link between work packages and resources.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":20,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>The iterative process of increasing the level of detail in a project management plan as more information becomes available is called:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The iterative process of increasing the level of detail in a project management plan as more information becomes available is called:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Continuous improvement<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Continuous improvement\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Predictive planning<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Predictive planning\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Progressive elaboration<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Progressive elaboration\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Quality assurance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Quality assurance\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C Progressive Elaboration is the iterative process of adding detail to the project management plan as more specific information becomes available.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Continuous Improvement focuses on ongoing enhancements but is not specific to planning.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Predictive Planning involves planning based on known and understood outcomes, not iterative detailing.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Quality Assurance is about ensuring quality standards are met, not about planning details.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Progressive Elaboration is the iterative process of adding detail to the project management plan as more specific information becomes available. Option A: Continuous Improvement focuses on ongoing enhancements but is not specific to planning. Option B: Predictive Planning involves planning based on known and understood outcomes, not iterative detailing. Option D: Quality Assurance is about ensuring quality standards are met, not about planning details.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":21,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>An effective conflict resolution technique that integrates multiple viewpoints to reach consensus and commitment is:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"An effective conflict resolution technique that integrates multiple viewpoints to reach consensus and commitment is:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Acceptance/Accommodation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Acceptance/Accommodation\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Force/Competition<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Force/Competition\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Collaboration/Problem Solving<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Collaboration/Problem Solving\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Compromise/Reconciliation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Compromise/Reconciliation\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C Collaboration/Problem Solving is the most effective conflict resolution technique as it involves working together to integrate multiple viewpoints and reach a consensus that all parties are committed to .<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Acceptance/Accommodation involves giving in to others' demands to maintain harmony, which may not resolve the underlying conflict.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Force/Competition is about asserting one’s viewpoint at the expense of others, which may not lead to consensus.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Compromise/Reconciliation involves finding a middle ground, but it may not fully satisfy all parties.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Collaboration/Problem Solving is the most effective conflict resolution technique as it involves working together to integrate multiple viewpoints and reach a consensus that all parties are committed to . Option A: Acceptance/Accommodation involves giving in to others' demands to maintain harmony, which may not resolve the underlying conflict. Option B: Force/Competition is about asserting one’s viewpoint at the expense of others, which may not lead to consensus. Option D: Compromise/Reconciliation involves finding a middle ground, but it may not fully satisfy all parties.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":22,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A temporary endeavor creating a unique product, service, or result is called:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A temporary endeavor creating a unique product, service, or result is called:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Project\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Plan\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Product<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Product\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Prototyp<span><\\/span>e<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Prototyp e\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A A project is a temporary endeavor undertaken to create a unique product, service, or result.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> A plan is a document that outlines how a project will be executed, monitored, and controlled.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A A project is a temporary endeavor undertaken to create a unique product, service, or result. Option B: A plan is a document that outlines how a project will be executed, monitored, and controlled.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":23,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>The status of deliverables, implementation status for change requests, and forecasts to complete are examples of:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The status of deliverables, implementation status for change requests, and forecasts to complete are examples of:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Enterprise Environmental Factors<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Enterprise Environmental Factors\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Organizational Process Assets<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Organizational Process Assets\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Earned Value Management (EVM)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Earned Value Management (EVM)\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Work Performance Information<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Work Performance Information\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D Work Performance Information includes the status of deliverables, the implementation status of change requests, and forecasts to complete the project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Enterprise Environmental Factors are conditions that affect the project but are not under the control of the project team.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Organizational Process Assets include processes, policies, and knowledge bases specific to the performing organization.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Earned Value Management (EVM) is a technique that integrates project scope, schedule, and cost variables to assess project performance and progress.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Work Performance Information includes the status of deliverables, the implementation status of change requests, and forecasts to complete the project. Option A: Enterprise Environmental Factors are conditions that affect the project but are not under the control of the project team. Option B: Organizational Process Assets include processes, policies, and knowledge bases specific to the performing organization. Option C: Earned Value Management (EVM) is a technique that integrates project scope, schedule, and cost variables to assess project performance and progress.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":24,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">When can a Sprint be canceled by the Development Team?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"When can a Sprint be canceled by the Development Team?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>When user stories are not well understood<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. When user stories are not well understood\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>When the sprint backlog items become unachievable<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. When the sprint backlog items become unachievable\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>When the Product Owner is not available enough<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. When the Product Owner is not available enough\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>When key members of the Development Team are on leave<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. When key members of the Development Team are on leave\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Only the Product Owners can cancel Sprints<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Only the Product Owners can cancel Sprints\"}],\"key\":[\"E\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = E<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Only the Product Owner has the authority to cancel the Sprint. The Product Owner may do so from the influence of stakeholders, the Development Team, or the Scrum Master.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = E Only the Product Owner has the authority to cancel the Sprint. The Product Owner may do so from the influence of stakeholders, the Development Team, or the Scrum Master.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":25,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which process group focuses on establishing the scope of the project, refining the objectives, and defining the course of action required to achieve the project’s objectives:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which process group focuses on establishing the scope of the project, refining the objectives, and defining the course of action required to achieve the project’s objectives:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Planning<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Planning\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Executing<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Executing\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Monitoring and Controlling<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Monitoring and Controlling\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Closing<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Closing\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A The Planning process group focuses on establishing the project’s scope, refining objectives, and defining the course of action required to achieve the project’s objectives.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The Executing process group involves performing the work defined in the project management plan.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The Monitoring and Controlling process group involves tracking, reviewing, and regulating the progress of the project<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The Closing process group involves finalizing all activities across all project management process groups.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The Planning process group focuses on establishing the project’s scope, refining objectives, and defining the course of action required to achieve the project’s objectives. Option B: The Executing process group involves performing the work defined in the project management plan. Option C: The Monitoring and Controlling process group involves tracking, reviewing, and regulating the progress of the project . Option D: The Closing process group involves finalizing all activities across all project management process groups.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":26,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>When should a Sprint Retrospective be held?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"When should a Sprint Retrospective be held?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Between the Sprint Planning and the Sprint Review<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Between the Sprint Planning and the Sprint Review\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>At the end of each Sprint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. At the end of each Sprint\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Upon the Product Owner’s request<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Upon the Product Owner’s request\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>At the beginning of each Sprint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. At the beginning of each Sprint\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B A Sprint Retrospective should be held at the end of each sprint, after the Sprint Review and before the next Sprint Planning. This meeting allows the team to reflect on the sprint, discuss what went well and what didn&#x27;t, and identify improvements for the next sprint.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B A Sprint Retrospective should be held at the end of each sprint, after the Sprint Review and before the next Sprint Planning. This meeting allows the team to reflect on the sprint, discuss what went well and what didn't, and identify improvements for the next sprint.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":27,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>When is the Sprint Backlog created?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"When is the Sprint Backlog created?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>During the Sprint Planning meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. During the Sprint Planning meeting\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Before the Sprint Planning meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Before the Sprint Planning meeting\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>During the Sprint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. During the Sprint\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>At the start of the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. At the start of the project\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A The Sprint Backlog consists of selected Product Backlog items for the Sprint, along with a plan to deliver the product increment and achieve the Sprint Goal. It’s created during the Sprint Planning meeting.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The product backlog is created at the start of the project, not the sprint backlog.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The Sprint Backlog consists of selected Product Backlog items for the Sprint, along with a plan to deliver the product increment and achieve the Sprint Goal. It’s created during the Sprint Planning meeting. Option D: The product backlog is created at the start of the project, not the sprint backlog.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":28,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A project manager is about to close a project. What should the project manager use?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is about to close a project. What should the project manager use?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Accepted deliverable<span><\\/span>s<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Accepted deliverable s\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Final product or service<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Final product or service\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Updated lessons learned register<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Updated lessons learned register\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Final report<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Final report\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A Accepted deliverables are input to the Close Project or Phase process, ensuring that the deliverables meet the requirements and have been accepted by the customer.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Options B, C, D:<\\/span> All these artifacts: Final product or service, Updated lessons learned register, and Final report are outputs of the project closure process.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Accepted deliverables are input to the Close Project or Phase process, ensuring that the deliverables meet the requirements and have been accepted by the customer. Options B, C, D: All these artifacts: Final product or service, Updated lessons learned register, and Final report are outputs of the project closure process.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":29,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">What does a Scrum Team consist of? (Select three)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What does a Scrum Team consist of? (Select three)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>1 to 10 Users<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. 1 to 10 Users\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>3 to 9 Developers<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. 3 to 9 Developers\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>One Sponsor<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. One Sponsor\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>One Product Owner<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. One Product Owner\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>One Business Analyst<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. One Business Analyst\"},{\"id\":\"F\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>F.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>One Scrum Master<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"F. One Scrum Master\"}],\"key\":[\"B\",\"D\",\"F\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B, D, F<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The Scrum Team consists of one Scrum Master, one Product Owner, and Developers.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B, D, F The Scrum Team consists of one Scrum Master, one Product Owner, and Developers.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":3},{\"n\":30,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>External organizations that maintain special relationships with the company and provide specialized expertise are called:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"External organizations that maintain special relationships with the company and provide specialized expertise are called:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Customers<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Customers\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Vendors<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Vendors\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Business partners<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Business partners\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Functional managers<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Functional managers\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C Business Partners are external organizations that maintain a special relationship with the company and provide specialized expertise, services, or resources.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Customers are the recipients of the project’s deliverables.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Vendors provide goods or services but do not necessarily have a special, ongoing relationship with the company.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Functional Managers are internal managers responsible for a specific department or function within the company.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Business Partners are external organizations that maintain a special relationship with the company and provide specialized expertise, services, or resources. Option A: Customers are the recipients of the project’s deliverables. Option B: Vendors provide goods or services but do not necessarily have a special, ongoing relationship with the company. Option D: Functional Managers are internal managers responsible for a specific department or function within the company.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":31,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which of the following best represents the role of a program manager?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following best represents the role of a program manager?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Delivering a specific product or service within budget and time constraints.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Delivering a specific product or service within budget and time constraints.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Overseeing several related projects to ensure they contribute to broader organizational goals.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Overseeing several related projects to ensure they contribute to broader organizational goals.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Managing all organizational initiatives to align with corporate strategy.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Managing all organizational initiatives to align with corporate strategy.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Supervising a single project through its completion.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Supervising a single project through its completion.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B A program manager is responsible for managing a collection of related projects (a program) that work together to deliver broader benefits and strategic value to the organization. The focus is on aligning these projects to contribute to larger organizational objectives, rather than focusing on just one project .<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Options A &amp; D:<\\/span> “Delivering a specific product or service within budget and time constraints” and “Supervising a single project through its completion” both describe the role of a project manager.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> “Managing all organizational initiatives to align with corporate strategy” describes the role of a portfolio manager.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B A program manager is responsible for managing a collection of related projects (a program) that work together to deliver broader benefits and strategic value to the organization. The focus is on aligning these projects to contribute to larger organizational objectives, rather than focusing on just one project . Options A & D: “Delivering a specific product or service within budget and time constraints” and “Supervising a single project through its completion” both describe the role of a project manager. Option C: “Managing all organizational initiatives to align with corporate strategy” describes the role of a portfolio manager.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":32,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>In a project, total float measures:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In a project, total float measures:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The ability to perform project activities in parallel to shorten the project duration.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The ability to perform project activities in parallel to shorten the project duration.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The time an activity can be extended or delayed without altering the project end date.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The time an activity can be extended or delayed without altering the project end date.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The time an activity can be shortened by adding more resources.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The time an activity can be shortened by adding more resources.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The total duration of the critical path.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The total duration of the critical path.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B Total float measures the amount of time an activity can be delayed without delaying the project&#x27;s end date.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> “The ability to perform project activities in parallel to shorten the project duration” is a description of the fast-tracking schedule compression technique, which is not related to float.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> “The time an activity can be shortened by adding more resources” describes crashing, a schedule compression technique.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The total duration of the critical path gives an estimation of the project duration.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Total float measures the amount of time an activity can be delayed without delaying the project's end date. Option A: “The ability to perform project activities in parallel to shorten the project duration” is a description of the fast-tracking schedule compression technique, which is not related to float. Option C: “The time an activity can be shortened by adding more resources” describes crashing, a schedule compression technique. Option D: The total duration of the critical path gives an estimation of the project duration.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":33,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which knowledge area includes the closing process group?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which knowledge area includes the closing process group?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project Quality Management<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Project Quality Management\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project Scope Management<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Project Scope Management\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project Procurement Management<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Project Procurement Management\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project Integration Management<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Project Integration Management\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D Project Integration Management includes the Closing Process Group, which involves finalizing all activities across all project management process groups.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Project Quality Management focuses on ensuring the project meets quality standards.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Project Scope Management focuses on defining and controlling what is included in the project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Project Procurement Management focuses on acquiring goods and services from outside the organization.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Project Integration Management includes the Closing Process Group, which involves finalizing all activities across all project management process groups. Option A: Project Quality Management focuses on ensuring the project meets quality standards. Option B: Project Scope Management focuses on defining and controlling what is included in the project. Option C: Project Procurement Management focuses on acquiring goods and services from outside the organization.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":34,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">What can be used to describe the role of a Product Owner?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What can be used to describe the role of a Product Owner?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A liaison between the team and the agile project manager.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. A liaison between the team and the agile project manager.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A messenger between the team and the stakeholders.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. A messenger between the team and the stakeholders.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A business analyst who is responsible for collecting requirements.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. A business analyst who is responsible for collecting requirements.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A project manager who oversees the product development.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. A project manager who oversees the product development.\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>A maximizer of business value.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. A maximizer of business value.\"}],\"key\":[\"E\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = E<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The Product Owner is responsible for maximizing the business value of the product resulting from the agile team's work. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = E The Product Owner is responsible for maximizing the business value of the product resulting from the agile team's work.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":35,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>What is the primary distinction between a project and operations?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is the primary distinction between a project and operations?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A project is continuous, while operations are temporary<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. A project is continuous, while operations are temporary\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Operations create unique outputs, while projects maintain existing systems<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Operations create unique outputs, while projects maintain existing systems\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Projects have a defined start and end, while operations are ongoing and repetitive<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Projects have a defined start and end, while operations are ongoing and repetitive\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Operations are riskier than projects<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Operations are riskier than projects\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C A project is a temporary endeavor with a specific beginning and end, aimed at producing a unique product, service, or result. Once the project goals are achieved, it is concluded. Operations, on the other hand, are ongoing and repetitive activities performed to maintain and sustain the organization&#x27;s day-to-day business. They don&#x27;t have a defined start and end date, and their focus is on maintaining existing systems and processes.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C A project is a temporary endeavor with a specific beginning and end, aimed at producing a unique product, service, or result. Once the project goals are achieved, it is concluded. Operations, on the other hand, are ongoing and repetitive activities performed to maintain and sustain the organization's day-to-day business. They don't have a defined start and end date, and their focus is on maintaining existing systems and processes.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":36,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which technique allows work to be executed at different levels of detail, depending on its position in the project lifecycle?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which technique allows work to be executed at different levels of detail, depending on its position in the project lifecycle?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sequence activities<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Sequence activities\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Dependency determination<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Dependency determination\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Requirements traceability matrix<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Requirements traceability matrix\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Rolling wave planning<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Rolling wave planning\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D Rolling Wave Planning is a technique that allows planning to be done in waves, with near-term work planned in detail and future work planned at a higher level.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Rolling Wave Planning is a technique that allows planning to be done in waves, with near-term work planned in detail and future work planned at a higher level.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":37,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">What should the team deliver at the end of a Sprint?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What should the team deliver at the end of a Sprint?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A software testing report requested by the Scrum Master<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. A software testing report requested by the Scrum Master\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A project status report requested by the executive management<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. A project status report requested by the executive management\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>An increment of working software that meets the Definition of Done<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. An increment of working software that meets the Definition of Done\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>An increment of software before testing<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. An increment of software before testing\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The agile team is responsible for delivering an increment of working software that meets the Definition of Done. The Definition of Done creates a shared understanding of what activities should be completed for an increment to be accepted.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The agile team is responsible for delivering an increment of working software that meets the Definition of Done. The Definition of Done creates a shared understanding of what activities should be completed for an increment to be accepted.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":38,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which of the following techniques can be used to assess whether requirements are aligned with the product&#x27;s objectives?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following techniques can be used to assess whether requirements are aligned with the product's objectives?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Use cases<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Use cases\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Context diagrams<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Context diagrams\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Activity network diagrams<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Activity network diagrams\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Five whys<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Five whys\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A Use cases describe how a system interacts with external entities (like users or other systems) to achieve specific goals. They help ensure that the requirements directly support the business objectives, making them the most suitable technique for this purpose.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Use cases describe how a system interacts with external entities (like users or other systems) to achieve specific goals. They help ensure that the requirements directly support the business objectives, making them the most suitable technique for this purpose.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":39,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A business analyst has been tasked with developing a business case for a new portfolio management system. Which of the following elements will the business analyst need to include as input?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A business analyst has been tasked with developing a business case for a new portfolio management system. Which of the following elements will the business analyst need to include as input?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s54E\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project budget <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Project budget\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Situation statemen<span><\\/span>t<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Situation statemen t\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Work breakdown structure<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Work breakdown structure\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Product scope<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Product scope\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B The situation statement describes the current state of affairs, the problem or opportunity, and the need for the new system. It sets the context for why the project is needed and what it aims to address, making it a crucial part of the business case.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> While important for the project planning phase, the project budget is not typically included in the initial business case. The business case focuses more on the justification and rationale for the project rather than detailed financial planning.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The WBS is a project management tool used to break down the project's deliverables into smaller, manageable components. It is developed later in the project planning phase, not typically included in the initial business case.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The product scope is an output rather than an input to the business case.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The situation statement describes the current state of affairs, the problem or opportunity, and the need for the new system. It sets the context for why the project is needed and what it aims to address, making it a crucial part of the business case. Option A: While important for the project planning phase, the project budget is not typically included in the initial business case. The business case focuses more on the justification and rationale for the project rather than detailed financial planning. Option C: The WBS is a project management tool used to break down the project's deliverables into smaller, manageable components. It is developed later in the project planning phase, not typically included in the initial business case. Option D: The product scope is an output rather than an input to the business case.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":40,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Who is responsible for engaging internal stakeholders and customers in Scrum?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Who is responsible for engaging internal stakeholders and customers in Scrum?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The Scrum Master<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The Scrum Master\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The Project Manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The Project Manager\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The Business Analyst<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The Business Analyst\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The Product Owner<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The Product Owner\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D In Scrum, the Product Owner is responsible for engaging all stakeholders, including the customers and/or end users.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D In Scrum, the Product Owner is responsible for engaging all stakeholders, including the customers and/or end users.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":41,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">During the sprint planning, the team decomposed a user story into four tasks. When working on the user story, a team member identified a fifth task. What should the team member do?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During the sprint planning, the team decomposed a user story into four tasks. When working on the user story, a team member identified a fifth task. What should the team member do?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Update the user story and work on the new task<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Update the user story and work on the new task\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Report the issue to the Scrum Master<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Report the issue to the Scrum Master\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Request from the product owner to approve the new task<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Request from the product owner to approve the new task\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Add the task to the product backlog<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Add the task to the product backlog\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The project team is responsible for how to do the work. Therefore, if a new task is identified within the user story it could be immediately added.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The situation doesn’t involve any issue. The team member can add, adjust, or remove tasks in order to deliver the user story according to its acceptance criteria.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The new task doesn’t require the product owner's approval since it’s a technical component of an agreed-upon user story<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> If the task represents a new feature or doesn’t contribute to the validation of the user story, then it should be added to the product backlog. In the described scenario, however, the task is an integral part of the user story.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The project team is responsible for how to do the work. Therefore, if a new task is identified within the user story it could be immediately added. Option B: The situation doesn’t involve any issue. The team member can add, adjust, or remove tasks in order to deliver the user story according to its acceptance criteria. Option C: The new task doesn’t require the product owner's approval since it’s a technical component of an agreed-upon user story . Option D: If the task represents a new feature or doesn’t contribute to the validation of the user story, then it should be added to the product backlog. In the described scenario, however, the task is an integral part of the user story.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":42,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which of the following extends the description of the activity by identifying the multiple components associated with each activity:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following extends the description of the activity by identifying the multiple components associated with each activity:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project document updates<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Project document updates\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Activity list<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Activity list\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Activity attributes<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Activity attributes\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project schedules<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Project schedules\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C Activity Attributes extend the description of the activity by identifying multiple components associated with each activity, such as predecessors, successors, logical relationships, and resource requirements.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Project Document Updates could include various changes to project documents but are not specific to activity descriptions.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The Activity List is a detailed list of activities to be performed but does not provide additional descriptive details.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Project Schedules provide timing information for activities, not detailed descriptions.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Activity Attributes extend the description of the activity by identifying multiple components associated with each activity, such as predecessors, successors, logical relationships, and resource requirements. Option A: Project Document Updates could include various changes to project documents but are not specific to activity descriptions. Option B: The Activity List is a detailed list of activities to be performed but does not provide additional descriptive details. Option D: Project Schedules provide timing information for activities, not detailed descriptions.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":43,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A key input to the stakeholder identification process is:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A key input to the stakeholder identification process is:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project Management Plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Project Management Plan\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder Register<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Stakeholder Register\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project Charter<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Project Charter\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder Analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Stakeholder Analysis\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C The Project Charter is a key input to the stakeholder identification process, as it provides high-level project information and identifies initial stakeholders.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The Project Management Plan is developed after stakeholders are identified.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The Stakeholder Register is an output of the stakeholder identification process, not an input.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Stakeholder Analysis is a tool used during the stakeholder identification process but not an input.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The Project Charter is a key input to the stakeholder identification process, as it provides high-level project information and identifies initial stakeholders. Option A: The Project Management Plan is developed after stakeholders are identified. Option B: The Stakeholder Register is an output of the stakeholder identification process, not an input. Option D: Stakeholder Analysis is a tool used during the stakeholder identification process but not an input.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":44,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>“Identify Risks” is part of which process group:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"“Identify Risks” is part of which process group:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Planning<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Planning\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Execution<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Execution\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Closing<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Closing\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Initiating<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Initiating\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = A Identify Risks is part of the Planning process group, where risks are identified and documented as part of the project’s risk management plan.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The Execution process group involves carrying out the work defined in the project management plan.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The Closing process group involves finalizing all activities across the project to formally close the project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The Initiating process group involves defining and authorizing the project or project phase.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Identify Risks is part of the Planning process group, where risks are identified and documented as part of the project’s risk management plan. Option B: The Execution process group involves carrying out the work defined in the project management plan. Option C: The Closing process group involves finalizing all activities across the project to formally close the project. Option D: The Initiating process group involves defining and authorizing the project or project phase.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":45,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">What should the Development Team do during the first Sprint? (Select two<span><\\/span>)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What should the Development Team do during the first Sprint? (Select two )\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Develop a plan for the rest of the project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Develop a plan for the rest of the project.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Analyze and document the requirements of the subsequent Sprint.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Analyze and document the requirements of the subsequent Sprint.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Develop at least one or two functionalities.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Develop at least one or two functionalities.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Analyze, design, and describe the full architecture of the software.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Analyze, design, and describe the full architecture of the software.\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Create a potentially shippable product increment.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Create a potentially shippable product increment.\"}],\"key\":[\"C\",\"E\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C &amp; E<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">On each sprint, the Development team is committed to creating one or a few functionalities and delivering a potentially shippable product increment<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C & E On each sprint, the Development team is committed to creating one or a few functionalities and delivering a potentially shippable product increment .\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":46,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A project team has identified several issues that could negatively impact the project delivery. The project manager is analyzing these issues and their interrelationships to understand the project&#x27;s overall complexity and develop a plan to address the challenges. Which technique is the project manager using?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project team has identified several issues that could negatively impact the project delivery. The project manager is analyzing these issues and their interrelationships to understand the project's overall complexity and develop a plan to address the challenges. Which technique is the project manager using?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Problem-solving<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Problem-solving\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Design thinking<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Design thinking\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Systems thinking<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Systems thinking\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Numeracy<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Numeracy\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C Systems thinking involves understanding how various components and hindrances within a project interact with each other and affect the overall system. By examining how different challenges are related and contribute to the project&#x27;s complexity, the project manager can develop a comprehensive plan that addresses these interconnected issues.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Systems thinking involves understanding how various components and hindrances within a project interact with each other and affect the overall system. By examining how different challenges are related and contribute to the project's complexity, the project manager can develop a comprehensive plan that addresses these interconnected issues.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":47,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A logical relationship in which a &#x27;successor&#x27; activity cannot start until a &#x27;predecessor&#x27; activity finishes is called:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A logical relationship in which a 'successor' activity cannot start until a 'predecessor' activity finishes is called:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Start-to-Finish (SF)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Start-to-Finish (SF)\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Finish-to-Start (FS)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Finish-to-Start (FS)\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Start-to-Start (SS)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Start-to-Start (SS)\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Finish-to-Finish (FF)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Finish-to-Finish (FF)\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B Finish-to-Start (FS) is the most common logical relationship where the successor activity cannot start until the predecessor activity has finished.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Start-to-Finish (SF) is a rare relationship where the successor cannot finish until the predecessor starts.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Start-to-Start (SS) allows both activities to start simultaneously, but they don’t have to finish together.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Finish-to-Finish (FF) means both activities must finish together, regardless of when they start.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Finish-to-Start (FS) is the most common logical relationship where the successor activity cannot start until the predecessor activity has finished. Option A: Start-to-Finish (SF) is a rare relationship where the successor cannot finish until the predecessor starts. Option C: Start-to-Start (SS) allows both activities to start simultaneously, but they don’t have to finish together. Option D: Finish-to-Finish (FF) means both activities must finish together, regardless of when they start.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":48,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which type of contract allows both the seller and the buyer the opportunity to deviate from performance with financial incentives:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which type of contract allows both the seller and the buyer the opportunity to deviate from performance with financial incentives:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Time and Material (T&amp;M) with Price Indexing<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Time and Material (T&M) with Price Indexing\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Fixed-Price Incentive Fee (FPIF)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Fixed-Price Incentive Fee (FPIF)\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cost Plus Award Fee (CPAF)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Cost Plus Award Fee (CPAF)\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Time and Material (T&amp;M)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Time and Material (T&M)\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B Fixed-Price Incentive Fee (FPIF) contracts allow deviations from performance with financial incentives, encouraging the seller to meet or exceed certain performance targets.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Time and Material (T&amp;M) contracts are based on the actual time and materials used, not performance incentives.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Cost Plus Award Fee (CPAF) contracts include an award fee based on performance but do not allow the same flexibility as FPIF contracts.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Basic T&amp;M contracts do not include performance-based incentives.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Fixed-Price Incentive Fee (FPIF) contracts allow deviations from performance with financial incentives, encouraging the seller to meet or exceed certain performance targets. Option A: Time and Material (T&M) contracts are based on the actual time and materials used, not performance incentives. Option C: Cost Plus Award Fee (CPAF) contracts include an award fee based on performance but do not allow the same flexibility as FPIF contracts. Option D: Basic T&M contracts do not include performance-based incentives.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":49,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which of the following best describes the role of stakeholders in the creation of a product roadmap?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following best describes the role of stakeholders in the creation of a product roadmap?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholders are only involved in the execution phase of the product roadmap.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Stakeholders are only involved in the execution phase of the product roadmap.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholders provide input on product features, priorities, and timelines that should be reflected in the roadmap.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Stakeholders provide input on product features, priorities, and timelines that should be reflected in the roadmap.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholders are responsible for approving the final product roadmap.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Stakeholders are responsible for approving the final product roadmap.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholders are not typically involved in the creation of the product roadmap.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Stakeholders are not typically involved in the creation of the product roadmap.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B Stakeholders play a key role in the creation of a product roadmap by providing input on what features, priorities, and timelines should be included. Their feedback helps ensure that the roadmap aligns with their needs and expectations, and it guides the development process to meet the overall strategic goals of the organization.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Stakeholders being involved only in the execution phase is incorrect, as their involvement is crucial throughout the entire roadmap creation.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The product owner is responsible for developing the product roadmap and the sponsor is responsible for approving its final version<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Stakeholders not being typically involved is incorrect because stakeholder input is essential for creating a relevant and effective product roadmap.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Stakeholders play a key role in the creation of a product roadmap by providing input on what features, priorities, and timelines should be included. Their feedback helps ensure that the roadmap aligns with their needs and expectations, and it guides the development process to meet the overall strategic goals of the organization. Option A: Stakeholders being involved only in the execution phase is incorrect, as their involvement is crucial throughout the entire roadmap creation. Option C: The product owner is responsible for developing the product roadmap and the sponsor is responsible for approving its final version . Option D: Stakeholders not being typically involved is incorrect because stakeholder input is essential for creating a relevant and effective product roadmap.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":50,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>In eXtreme Programming, which of the following practices is NOT commonly used?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In eXtreme Programming, which of the following practices is NOT commonly used?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Pair Programmin<span><\\/span>g<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Pair Programmin g\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Test-Driven Development (TDD)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Test-Driven Development (TDD)\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Continuous Integration<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Continuous Integration\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Feature Team<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Feature Team\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D Feature team involves organizing teams based on specific features of a product. Feature team is used in Feature-driven development (FDD), and isn’t a common practice in XP. XP tends to focus more on practices like collective code ownership and maintaining a flat team structure rather than dividing teams by features.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Feature team involves organizing teams based on specific features of a product. Feature team is used in Feature-driven development (FDD), and isn’t a common practice in XP. XP tends to focus more on practices like collective code ownership and maintaining a flat team structure rather than dividing teams by features.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":51,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which method helps a group to generate the most ideas on a topic without evaluating their feasibility or practicality?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which method helps a group to generate the most ideas on a topic without evaluating their feasibility or practicality?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Interviewing<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Interviewing\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Prototyping<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Prototyping\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Surveying<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Surveying\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Brainstorming<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Brainstorming\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D Brainstorming is designed to generate a large number of ideas in a short period of time. During brainstorming, ideas are generated without immediate evaluation or judgment, which encourages creativity and the free flow of thoughts.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Interviewing involves asking individuals questions to gather information and insights. It focuses on collecting data and opinions rather than generating a wide range of ideas.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Surveying uses questionnaires or polls to gather information from a large group of people. It is useful for collecting opinions or feedback but is not specifically designed for idea generation.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Brainstorming is designed to generate a large number of ideas in a short period of time. During brainstorming, ideas are generated without immediate evaluation or judgment, which encourages creativity and the free flow of thoughts. Option A: Interviewing involves asking individuals questions to gather information and insights. It focuses on collecting data and opinions rather than generating a wide range of ideas. Option C: Surveying uses questionnaires or polls to gather information from a large group of people. It is useful for collecting opinions or feedback but is not specifically designed for idea generation.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":52,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A requirements traceability matrix (RTM) reveals that some requirements have not been tested. What should the business analyst do next?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A requirements traceability matrix (RTM) reveals that some requirements have not been tested. What should the business analyst do next?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Proceed with delivery and address the missing tests after the delivery.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Proceed with delivery and address the missing tests after the delivery.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Reassess the readiness for delivery and ensure that all requirements are tested and validated before proceeding.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Reassess the readiness for delivery and ensure that all requirements are tested and validated before proceeding.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Consider the missing tests as risks and update the risk register.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Consider the missing tests as risks and update the risk register.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Update the project budget to account for additional testing.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Update the project budget to account for additional testing.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B Ensuring that all requirements have been tested and validated is important before proceeding with delivery. The requirements traceability matrix (RTM) is used to ensure that every requirement is accounted for and tested. IF some requirements have not been accounted for, it’s important to address this before moving forward in order to avoid issues with the final product.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Proceeding with delivery and addressing the missing tests later could lead to unresolved issues and decreased product quality<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The missing tests should be performed. Therefore, it’s not appropriate to skip them and consider them as risks.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Updating the project budget to account for additional testing might be necessary if additional tests are required, but in this case reassessing the readiness for delivery is part of the project and not an additional requirement.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Ensuring that all requirements have been tested and validated is important before proceeding with delivery. The requirements traceability matrix (RTM) is used to ensure that every requirement is accounted for and tested. IF some requirements have not been accounted for, it’s important to address this before moving forward in order to avoid issues with the final product. Option A: Proceeding with delivery and addressing the missing tests later could lead to unresolved issues and decreased product quality Option C: The missing tests should be performed. Therefore, it’s not appropriate to skip them and consider them as risks. Option D: Updating the project budget to account for additional testing might be necessary if additional tests are required, but in this case reassessing the readiness for delivery is part of the project and not an additional requirement.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":53,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>The skills needed for a project manager to motivate and encourage a team member, actively listen to their concerns, and persuade them to take action, are called:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The skills needed for a project manager to motivate and encourage a team member, actively listen to their concerns, and persuade them to take action, are called:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Organizational Skills<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Organizational Skills\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Technical Skills<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Technical Skills\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Communication Skills<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Communication Skills\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Hard Skills<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Hard Skills\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C Communication Skills are critical for project managers to effectively manage teams, stakeholders, and project activities.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Organizational Skills involve structuring and managing resources and tasks but are not specifically related to motivating or <span><\\/span>encouraging.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Technical Skills are the specific knowledge and abilities related to the industry or discipline but do not include the soft skills mentioned.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Hard Skills refer to technical and administrative abilities, not the interpersonal skills needed for effective communication.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Communication Skills are critical for project managers to effectively manage teams, stakeholders, and project activities. Option A: Organizational Skills involve structuring and managing resources and tasks but are not specifically related to motivating or encouraging. Option B: Technical Skills are the specific knowledge and abilities related to the industry or discipline but do not include the soft skills mentioned. Option D: Hard Skills refer to technical and administrative abilities, not the interpersonal skills needed for effective communication.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":54,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Before moving forward to the development phase, the business analyst needs to ensure that all requirements are up to quality standards. What should the business analyst do?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Before moving forward to the development phase, the business analyst needs to ensure that all requirements are up to quality standards. What should the business analyst do?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Negotiate with the client to standardize the requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Negotiate with the client to standardize the requirements\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ask the quality team to redesign the requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Ask the quality team to redesign the requirements\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Verify requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Verify requirements\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Validate requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Validate requirements\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C Verifying requirements is the process of ensuring that all requirements are of a sufficient quality (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 175).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Requirements verification could be done via peer reviews, such as another business analyst, team lead, or quality control team member. However, asking the quality team to redesign the requirements means altering them, which is not appropriate.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Validating requirements is the process of checking that requirements meet business goals and objectives.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Verifying requirements is the process of ensuring that all requirements are of a sufficient quality (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 175). Option B: Requirements verification could be done via peer reviews, such as another business analyst, team lead, or quality control team member. However, asking the quality team to redesign the requirements means altering them, which is not appropriate. Option D: Validating requirements is the process of checking that requirements meet business goals and objectives.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":55,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which aspect of emotional intelligence involves the ability to regulate and control emotions?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which aspect of emotional intelligence involves the ability to regulate and control emotions?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Social skills<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Social skills\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Decision making<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Decision making\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Self-awareness<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Self-awareness\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Self-managemen<span><\\/span>t<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Self-managemen t\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D Self-management in emotional intelligence refers to the ability to regulate and control one&#x27;s emotions (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 26).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Self-awareness involves recognizing and understanding one's own emotions.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Self-management in emotional intelligence refers to the ability to regulate and control one's emotions (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 26). Option C: Self-awareness involves recognizing and understanding one's own emotions.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":56,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which Agile framework is most associated with the concept of &quot;sprints&quot;?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which Agile framework is most associated with the concept of \\\"sprints\\\"?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Lean<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Lean\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Crystal<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Crystal\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scrum<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Scrum\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>FDD<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. FDD\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Scrum is built around the concept of sprints, which are time-boxed iterations (usually 2-4 weeks) during which specific work is completed and made ready for review.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Lean focuses on eliminating waste and improving efficiency and does not specifically involve sprints.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Crystal framework emphasizes people and interaction and doesn’t have a formalized structure like sprints.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Feature-driven development (FDD) focuses on designing and building features and doesn’t use sprints.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Scrum is built around the concept of sprints, which are time-boxed iterations (usually 2-4 weeks) during which specific work is completed and made ready for review. Option A: Lean focuses on eliminating waste and improving efficiency and does not specifically involve sprints. Option B: Crystal framework emphasizes people and interaction and doesn’t have a formalized structure like sprints. Option D: Feature-driven development (FDD) focuses on designing and building features and doesn’t use sprints.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":57,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>The zero duration of milestones in project planning is because milestones:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The zero duration of milestones in project planning is because milestones:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Are unpredictable and could happen in no time.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Are unpredictable and could happen in no time.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Occur at random moments in the project lifecycle.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Occur at random moments in the project lifecycle.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Represent a moment in time, such as a significant project point or event.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Represent a moment in time, such as a significant project point or event.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Represent non-important points in the project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Represent non-important points in the project.\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C Milestones represent a moment in time, such as a significant project point or event, which is why they have zero duration.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> While milestones can be challenging, they are not unpredictable.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Milestones are planned and do not occur randomly<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Milestones are significant points, not non-significant, and are carefully planned in the project timeline.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Milestones represent a moment in time, such as a significant project point or event, which is why they have zero duration. Option A: While milestones can be challenging, they are not unpredictable. Option B: Milestones are planned and do not occur randomly . Option D: Milestones are significant points, not non-significant, and are carefully planned in the project timeline.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":58,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>After the implementation of the new system, a business analyst is planning to validate solution results to determine if it meets the expected objectives. What is the most effective technique for collecting feedback from users about their experience with the new system?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"After the implementation of the new system, a business analyst is planning to validate solution results to determine if it meets the expected objectives. What is the most effective technique for collecting feedback from users about their experience with the new system?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span><span>Organization modeling<\\/span><\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Organization modeling\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span><span>Survey<\\/span><\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Survey\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span><span>Focus group<\\/span><\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Focus group\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span><span>Interface analysis<\\/span><\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Interface analysis\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B Surveys are a direct method for collecting feedback from a large group of people efficiently. They can be designed to gather specific information about employees&#x27; experiences, satisfaction, and issues with the new system.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Organization modeling focuses on understanding and documenting the structure and relationships within an organization. It is not directly used for collecting feedback on system performance or user experience.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Focus groups bring together prequalified stakeholders and subject matter experts (SMEs) to learn about their expectations and attitudes about a proposed solution (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 247).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Interface analysis involves evaluating the design and usability of the system's user interface. While it can provide insights into how well the system meets design requirements, it doesn't gather user feedback on their overall experience.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Surveys are a direct method for collecting feedback from a large group of people efficiently. They can be designed to gather specific information about employees' experiences, satisfaction, and issues with the new system. Option A: Organization modeling focuses on understanding and documenting the structure and relationships within an organization. It is not directly used for collecting feedback on system performance or user experience. Option C: Focus groups bring together prequalified stakeholders and subject matter experts (SMEs) to learn about their expectations and attitudes about a proposed solution (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 247). Option D: Interface analysis involves evaluating the design and usability of the system's user interface. While it can provide insights into how well the system meets design requirements, it doesn't gather user feedback on their overall experience.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":59,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which group decision-making technique involves experts providing estimates in multiple rounds, followed by team discussions, to reach consensus?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which group decision-making technique involves experts providing estimates in multiple rounds, followed by team discussions, to reach consensus?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Nominal Group Technique<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Nominal Group Technique\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Majority<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Majority\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Delphi<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Delphi\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Multi-Criteria Decision Analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Multi-Criteria Decision Analysis\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The Delphi technique is a group decision-making process where subject matter experts provide estimates individually over several rounds. After each round, the estimates are discussed by the team, and the process repeats until a consensus is reached. (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 178)<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Nominal Group Technique is a group decision-making method where individuals generate ideas independently, then discuss them in a group, and finally rank them. However, it doesn’t involve multiple rounds of estimates or gradual consensus-building like the Delphi technique.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The majority decision-making technique involves voting where the option that receives more than half the votes wins.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Multi-Criteria Decision Analysis is a technique used to evaluate and prioritize options based on various criteria.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The Delphi technique is a group decision-making process where subject matter experts provide estimates individually over several rounds. After each round, the estimates are discussed by the team, and the process repeats until a consensus is reached. (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 178) Option A: Nominal Group Technique is a group decision-making method where individuals generate ideas independently, then discuss them in a group, and finally rank them. However, it doesn’t involve multiple rounds of estimates or gradual consensus-building like the Delphi technique. Option B: The majority decision-making technique involves voting where the option that receives more than half the votes wins. Option D: Multi-Criteria Decision Analysis is a technique used to evaluate and prioritize options based on various criteria.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":60,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">In Scrum, what sprint burndown chart is used to track?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"In Scrum, what sprint burndown chart is used to track?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The number of completed user stories in the sprint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The number of completed user stories in the sprint\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Work remaining in the sprint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Work remaining in the sprint\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The remaining sprints in the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The remaining sprints in the project\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The completed work in the sprint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The completed work in the sprint\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B A sprint burndown chart is a chart that shows the remaining amount in the sprint backlog. Time is shown on the horizontal axis and the remaining work on the vertical axis. As time progresses and items are drawn from the sprint backlog and completed, a plot line showing work remaining may be expected to fall.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B A sprint burndown chart is a chart that shows the remaining amount in the sprint backlog. Time is shown on the horizontal axis and the remaining work on the vertical axis. As time progresses and items are drawn from the sprint backlog and completed, a plot line showing work remaining may be expected to fall.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":61,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>To which interpersonal skill are job satisfaction, challenging work, and good financial compensation related ?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"To which interpersonal skill are job satisfaction, challenging work, and good financial compensation related ?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Influence<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Influence\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Motivation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Motivation\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Negotiation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Negotiation\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Emotional intelligence<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Emotional intelligence\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B Motivation involves ensuring that team members are satisfied with their job, feel challenged, and are compensated fairly, which helps keep them engaged and productive .<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Influence involves persuading others to act but does not directly relate to job satisfaction or compensation.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Negotiation involves reaching agreements that satisfy all parties, not specifically related to job satisfaction.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Motivation involves ensuring that team members are satisfied with their job, feel challenged, and are compensated fairly, which helps keep them engaged and productive . Option A: Influence involves persuading others to act but does not directly relate to job satisfaction or compensation. Option C: Negotiation involves reaching agreements that satisfy all parties, not specifically related to job satisfaction.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":62,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>A product backlog that contains unfinished high-priority items indicates that:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A product backlog that contains unfinished high-priority items indicates that:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The product is ready for delivery if all other items are complete.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The product is ready for delivery if all other items are complete.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The product may not be ready for delivery until all high-priority items are completed and accepted by stakeholders.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The product may not be ready for delivery until all high-priority items are completed and accepted by stakeholders.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project is on hold and will be resumed later<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The project is on hold and will be resumed later\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project team needs additional resources to complete the backlog items<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The project team needs additional resources to complete the backlog items\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B A product backlog is a prioritized list of work for the development team. High-priority items typically represent critical features or requirements that must be completed for the product to be considered ready for delivery. If high-priority items are unfinished, it indicates that the product may not be ready for delivery until these critical items are completed and accepted by stakeholders.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B A product backlog is a prioritized list of work for the development team. High-priority items typically represent critical features or requirements that must be completed for the product to be considered ready for delivery. If high-priority items are unfinished, it indicates that the product may not be ready for delivery until these critical items are completed and accepted by stakeholders.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":63,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>The following is a network diagram for a project. What is the project&#x27;s duration?<\\/p><div class=\\\"class_sFS-0\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/div>\",\"stemText\":\"The following is a network diagram for a project. What is the project's duration?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>8 days<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. 8 days\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>9 days<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. 9 days\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>10 days<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. 10 days\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>11 days<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. 11 days\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C The project’s duration is 10 days, which is calculated based on the critical path—the longest path through the network diagram, determining the shortest time to complete the project.<\\/p><div><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,";
